Upgrade version 1 bundles to the current checksum version.

Version 1 bundle checksums ignored file names. Migrating verifies the files
against the existing manifest, then recomputes the checksum so it covers file
names and contents. The title, author, creation time and tags are preserved.
The bundle checksum changes.

A corrupted bundle is refused. Files that version 1 skipped because their path
contained ".bundle" are added; any other unlisted file is refused.

With --pool, every version 1 bundle in the pool is migrated and its directory
renamed to the new checksum. An entry whose new checksum is already in the pool
is left in place and reported.

Examples:
  # Migrate one bundle
  bundle migrate /path/to/bundle

  # Migrate all bundles in a pool
  bundle migrate --pool default
